<table class="fourier-table">
  <caption>Alguns pares de transformadas de Fourier</caption>
  <tr>
    <th>$f(t)$</th>
    <th>$F(\omega)$</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>$\delta(t)$</td>
    <td>$1$</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>$\delta(t-a)$</td>
    <td>$e^{-ia\omega}$</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>$u(t)$</td>
    <td>$\pi\delta(\omega) + \dfrac{1}{i\omega}$</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>$1$</td>
    <td>$2\pi\delta(\omega)$</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>$\operatorname{sgn}(t)$</td>
    <td>$\dfrac{2}{i\omega}$</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>$e^{i\omega_0 t}$</td>
    <td>$2\pi\delta(\omega-\omega_0)$</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>$\cos\omega_0 t$</td>
    <td>$\pi(\delta(\omega-\omega_0)+\delta(\omega+\omega_0))$</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>$\operatorname{sen}\omega_0 t$</td>
    <td>$\dfrac{\pi}{i}(\delta(\omega-\omega_0)-\delta(\omega+\omega_0))$</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>$\operatorname{rect}\left(\dfrac{t}{a}\right)$</td>
    <td>$|a|\cdot \operatorname{sinc}\left(a\dfrac{\omega}{2\pi}\right) \;=\; \dfrac{2}{\omega}\operatorname{sen}\left(\dfrac{\omega}{a}\right)$</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>$\cos(\omega_0 t)u(t)$</td>
    <td>$\dfrac{\pi}{2}(\delta(\omega-\omega_0)+\delta(\omega+\omega_0)) + \dfrac{i\omega}{\omega_0^2-\omega^2}$</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>$\operatorname{sen}(\omega_0 t)u(t)$</td>
    <td>$\dfrac{\pi}{2i}(\delta(\omega-\omega_0)-\delta(\omega+\omega_0)) + \dfrac{\omega^2}{\omega_0^2-\omega^2}$</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>$\operatorname{rect}(t/a)\cos(\omega_0 t)$</td>
    <td>$a\left(\operatorname{sinc}\dfrac{(\omega-\omega_0)a}{2\pi} + \operatorname{sinc}\dfrac{(\omega+\omega_0)a}{2\pi}\right)$</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>$\operatorname{sinc}\left(\dfrac{t}{a}\right)$</td>
    <td>$|a|\cdot \operatorname{rect}\left(\dfrac{\omega}{2\pi a}\right)$</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>$\operatorname{sinc}^2\left(\dfrac{t}{a}\right)$</td>
    <td>$|a|\cdot \operatorname{tri}\left(\dfrac{\omega}{2\pi a}\right)$</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>$e^{-at}u(t), \operatorname{Re}(a)>0$</td>
    <td>$\dfrac{1}{a+i\omega}$</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>$t^n$</td>
    <td>$2\pi i^n \delta^n(\omega)$</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>$t^{n-1}e^{-at}u(t), \operatorname{Re}(a)>0$</td>
    <td>$\dfrac{(n-1)!}{(a+i\omega)^n}$</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>$e^{-a|t|}, \operatorname{Re}(a)>0$</td>
    <td>$\dfrac{2a}{a^2+\omega^2}$</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>$e^{-\pi t^2}$</td>
    <td>$e^{-\frac{\omega^2}{4\pi}}$</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>$\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{|t|}}$</td>
    <td>$\sqrt{\dfrac{2\pi}{|\omega|}}$</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>$\dfrac{1}{t^2+a^2}$</td>
    <td>$\dfrac{\pi}{a}e^{-a|\omega|}$</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>$\operatorname{tri}(t)$</td>
    <td>$\operatorname{sinc}^2\left(\dfrac{\omega}{2\pi}\right)$</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2>Transformadas operacionais</h2>
<p>As transformadas de Fourier, assim como as de Laplace, podem ser classificadas como funcionais e operacionais.</p>

